## Summary

I built the **`SearchInput` P4 Apple shared surface** — a complete, native SwiftUI parity of `components/forms/SearchInput.tsx` — as 11 files in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/`:

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `SearchInput.swift` | Public surface view + web-prop convenience init |
| `SearchInput.Adapter.swift` | Pure core: history reducer (`searchHistory.ts` port), keyboard clamps, a11y label |
| `SearchInput.Projection.swift` | Connectivity/load-status/snapshot/resolved + projection |
| `SearchInput.Model.swift` | `@Observable` P1/S8 state-holder, P1/S11 telemetry, P1/S10 facade |
| `SearchInput.Seams.swift` | Source protocol + UserDefaults/in-memory history stores + Live/InMemory sources |
| `SearchInput.States.swift` / `.Views.swift` | Leaf chrome + field editor, history panel/rows, freshness chip |
| `.Previews` / `.Tests` / `.AdapterTests` / `.strings` | Per-state previews, 47 tests, i18n catalog |

**Parity delivered:** debounced controlled field, clear button, focus-revealed recent-searches dropdown (select/remove/clear-all + arrow/enter/escape keyboard nav), focus-guard buffer re-sync, all i18n keys (`common.clear`, `search.history.title/removeAria/clear`), every state (loading/empty/error/data + stale/offline), and VoiceOver labels on every control.

